/**
\page page_stgmtcollection StGmtCollection — GMT Collection Documentation

\brief Top-level event container for all Global Muon Tracker (GMT) data in StEvent.

\section gmt_overview Overview

\ref StGmtCollection is the root-level container that aggregates all Global Muon Tracker
(GMT) data for a single STAR event.  The GMT is a GEM-based detector providing muon
identification and tracking.  It is composed of **8 modules** (\c kGmtNumModules = 8),
each with **2 readout layers** (\c kGmtNumLayers = 2 — one X-strip layer and one Y-pad
layer) and **128 channels per layer** (\c kGmtNumStrips = 128).

Three levels of reconstruction are represented:

- **Strip** (\ref StGmtStrip) — individual 1D readout channel carrying raw ADC and
  calibration data.
- **Hit** (\ref StGmtHit) — a 1D cluster of adjacent strips within one layer of one
  module.
- **Point** (\ref StGmtPoint) — a 2D reconstructed position formed by pairing an
  X-layer hit and a Y-layer hit.

\section gmt_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

All four collection classes derive directly from \c StObject:

\code
StObject
└── StGmtCollection           (top-level event container)
    ├── StGmtStripCollection  (embedded array[kGmtNumModules=8])
    ├── StGmtHitCollection    (embedded array[kGmtNumModules=8])
    └── StGmtPointCollection  (single embedded instance)
\endcode

\section gmt_containment Containment Model

\code
StGmtCollection
│
├── mStripCollection[8]  : StGmtStripCollection
│   ├── mModule            : Short_t
│   ├── mStripVec          : StSPtrVecGmtStrip   (owns StGmtStrip objects)
│   ├── mStripElecIdVec    : StPtrVecGmtStrip    (transient, not streamed)
│   └── mStripGeoIdVec     : StPtrVecGmtStrip    (transient, not streamed)
│
├── mHitCollection[8]    : StGmtHitCollection
│   ├── mModule            : Short_t
│   └── mHitVec            : StSPtrVecGmtHit     (owns StGmtHit objects)
│
└── mPointCollection     : StGmtPointCollection
    └── mPointVec          : StSPtrVecGmtPoint   (owns StGmtPoint objects)
\endcode

Key constants from \c StEnumerations.h:

| Constant | Value | Meaning |
|----------|-------|---------|
| \c kGmtNumModules       | 8    | Total GMT detector modules |
| \c kGmtNumLayers        | 2    | Readout layers per module (X + Y) |
| \c kGmtNumStrips        | 128  | Channels per layer per module |
| \c kGmtNumStripsPerModule | 256 | Total strips per module |
| \c kGmtNumGeoIds        | 2048 | Total geometry IDs across all modules and layers |

\section gmt_ownership Object Ownership

- All sub-collections (\ref StGmtStripCollection, \ref StGmtHitCollection,
  \ref StGmtPointCollection) are **stack-allocated** (embedded) inside
  \ref StGmtCollection; callers must not delete them.
- Each sub-collection holds an \c StSPtrVec (smart-pointer vector) that **owns** its
  leaf objects.  The vector's destructor and \c clear() both delete the pointed-to
  objects.
- \ref StGmtStripCollection holds two additional plain-pointer vectors,
  \c mStripElecIdVec and \c mStripGeoIdVec, for fast transient lookup.  They are not
  written to the persistent store and do not own strips.  \c mStripGeoIdVec is sized
  to \c kGmtNumGeoIds at construction.
- \ref StGmtCollection itself is owned by the StEvent framework (St_DataSet /
  StXRefMain); its destructor is a no-op.
- **Do not delete** any pointer returned by getStripCollection(), getHitCollection(),
  getPointCollection(), getStrip(), getSortedStrip(), or any element from the
  \c StSPtrVec vectors.

\section gmt_datamembers Data Members

\subsection gmt_dm_top StGmtCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StGmtStripCollection[8] | \c mStripCollection | Strip collections, one per module (0-based) |
| \c StGmtHitCollection[8]   | \c mHitCollection   | Hit collections, one per module |
| \c StGmtPointCollection    | \c mPointCollection | 2D point collection for all modules |

\subsection gmt_dm_strip StGmtStripCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c Short_t           | \c mModule          | GMT module index (0–7) |
| \c StSPtrVecGmtStrip | \c mStripVec        | Persistent, owned strip vector |
| \c StPtrVecGmtStrip  | \c mStripElecIdVec  | Transient lookup by electronics ID (not streamed) |
| \c StPtrVecGmtStrip  | \c mStripGeoIdVec   | Transient lookup by geometry ID; sized to \c kGmtNumGeoIds (not streamed) |

\subsection gmt_dm_hit StGmtHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c Short_t          | \c mModule  | GMT module index (0–7) |
| \c StSPtrVecGmtHit  | \c mHitVec  | Persistent, owned hit vector |

\subsection gmt_dm_point StGmtPointCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StSPtrVecGmtPoint | \c mPointVec | Persistent, owned 2D-point vector |

\section gmt_methods Key Methods

\subsection gmt_meth_top StGmtCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c getNumModules() const | Returns \c kGmtNumModules (8) |
| \c getNumStrips() const | Total strips across all modules |
| \c getNumStrips(unsigned\ short\ module) const | Strips in one module |
| \c getNumHits() const | Total hits across all modules |
| \c getNumHits(unsigned\ short\ module) const | Hits in one module |
| \c getNumPoints() const | Total 2D points |
| \c getStripCollection(unsigned\ short) | Strip collection for module; \c nullptr if out of range |
| \c getHitCollection(unsigned\ short) | Hit collection for module; \c nullptr if out of range |
| \c getPointCollection() | Pointer to the point collection |
| \c Clear(Option_t*) | Clears all sub-collections (framework callback) |

\subsection gmt_meth_strip StGmtStripCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c getStrip(int\ id) | Returns or creates the strip for a geometry ID — the only way to add strips |
| \c getSortedStrip(int\ id) | Returns the strip at vector index \c id after sorting; logs error if null |
| \c getStripVec() | Direct access to the persistent strip vector |
| \c sortByGeoId() | Sorts the strip vector by geometry ID |
| \c sortByLayer() | Sorts the strip vector by layer (X strips first, then Y) |
| \c sortByCoord() | Sorts the strip vector by coordinate number |
| \c partialSortByCoord() | Partial sort of the first \c kGmtNumStrips elements by coordinate |
| \c removeFlagged() | Removes strips with negative geoIds |
| \c getNumStrips() const | Number of strips |
| \c getModule() / setModule() | Get/set module index |

\subsection gmt_meth_hit StGmtHitCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c getHitVec() | Reference to the owned hit vector |
| \c getNumHits() const | Number of hits |
| \c getModule() / setModule() | Get/set module index |

\subsection gmt_meth_point StGmtPointCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c getPointVec() | Reference to the owned point vector |
| \c getNumPoints() const | Number of 2D points |

\section gmt_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
// Obtain StGmtCollection from StEvent
StGmtCollection* gmtColl = event->gmtCollection();
if (!gmtColl) return;

// --- Strips ---
for (unsigned short mod = 0; mod < gmtColl->getNumModules(); ++mod) {
    const StGmtStripCollection* sc = gmtColl->getStripCollection(mod);
    if (!sc) continue;
    const StSPtrVecGmtStrip& strips = sc->getStripVec();
    for (const StGmtStrip* strip : strips) {
        if (!strip) continue;
        // strip->getGeoId(), strip->getAdc(), strip->isY(), ...
    }
}

// --- Hits ---
for (unsigned short mod = 0; mod < gmtColl->getNumModules(); ++mod) {
    const StGmtHitCollection* hc = gmtColl->getHitCollection(mod);
    if (!hc) continue;
    const StSPtrVecGmtHit& hits = hc->getHitVec();
    for (const StGmtHit* hit : hits) {
        if (!hit) continue;
        // hit->position(), hit->charge(), ...
    }
}

// --- 2D Points ---
const StGmtPointCollection* pc = gmtColl->getPointCollection();
if (pc) {
    const StSPtrVecGmtPoint& points = pc->getPointVec();
    for (const StGmtPoint* pt : points) {
        if (!pt) continue;
        // pt->position(), pt->charge(), ...
    }
}
\endcode

\warning Never call \c push_back() on the vector returned by \c getStripVec().
         Always use \ref StGmtStripCollection::getStrip(int) to insert new strips.
         The \c id argument to \c getStrip() is a **geometry ID**, unlike the FGT
         counterpart which uses an electronics ID.

*/
